the text of "26 USC 152(c)(4)(B)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/152/c.yaml".

the text of "26 USC 152(c)(1)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/152/c.yaml".

the text of "26 USC 152(c)(4)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/152/c.yaml".

the text of "26 USC 152(c)(1), 152(c)(4)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/152/c.yaml".

the abode fraction threshold is a number N if
    N = 1 / 2.

the support fraction threshold is a number N if
    N = 1 / 2.

the child age limit is 19, as stated in "26 USC 152(c)(3)(A)(i)".

the student age limit is 24, as stated in "26 USC 152(c)(3)(A)(ii)".

rule qualifying_child_relationship_1 with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(2)":
a person is qualifying child relationship if
    the individual of the person is child of taxpayer or descendant of such child.

rule qualifying_child_relationship_2 with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(2)":
a person is qualifying child relationship if
    the individual of the person is sibling stepsibling or descendant of such relative.

rule age_requirements_met_1 with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(3)":
a person is age requirements met if
    the individual of the person is permanently and totally disabled.

rule age_requirements_met_2 with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(3)":
a person is age requirements met if
    the individual of the person is younger than taxpayer
    and the individual age at close of calendar year of the person is a number N
    and the child age limit is a number M
    and N < M.

rule age_requirements_met_3 with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(3)":
a person is age requirements met if
    the individual of the person is younger than taxpayer
    and the individual of the person is student
    and the individual age at close of calendar year of the person is a number N
    and the student age limit is a number M
    and N < M.

rule individual_filed_joint_return_with_spouse_other_than_only_for_claim_of_refund with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(1)(E), 6013":
a person is individual filed joint return with spouse other than only for claim of refund if
    the filing status of the person is a code C
    and C = 1
    and it is not the case that the person is return filed only for claim of refund.

rule parents_claiming_child_do_not_file_joint_return_together with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(4)(B)":
a person is parents claiming child do not file joint return together if
    the parents filing status of the person is a code C
    and it is not the case that C = 1.

rule qualifying_child_before_tiebreaker with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(1)":
a person is qualifying child before tiebreaker if
    the person is qualifying child relationship
    and the individual principal place of abode with taxpayer fraction of the person is a rate R
    and the abode fraction threshold is a number N
    and R > N
    and the person is age requirements met
    and the individual own support fraction provided by individual of the person is a rate M
    and the support fraction threshold is a number K
    and M <= K
    and it is not the case that the person is individual filed joint return with spouse other than only for claim of refund.

rule tiebreaker_treats_individual_as_qualifying_child_of_taxpayer_1 with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(4)":
a person is tiebreaker treats individual as qualifying child of taxpayer if
    the person is a person
    and it is not the case that the individual of the person may be claimed as qualifying child by two or more taxpayers.

rule tiebreaker_treats_individual_as_qualifying_child_of_taxpayer_2 with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(4)":
a person is tiebreaker treats individual as qualifying child of taxpayer if
    the individual of the person may be claimed as qualifying child by two or more taxpayers
    and the parents of individual of the person may claim individual but no parent claims
    and it is not the case that the taxpayer of the person is parent of individual
    and the person is taxpayer adjusted gross income higher than highest parent adjusted gross income.

rule tiebreaker_treats_individual_as_qualifying_child_of_taxpayer_3 with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(4)":
a person is tiebreaker treats individual as qualifying child of taxpayer if
    the individual of the person may be claimed as qualifying child by two or more taxpayers
    and it is not the case that the parents of individual of the person may claim individual but no parent claims
    and the person is parents claiming child do not file joint return together
    and the taxpayer of the person is parent of individual
    and the person is child resided with taxpayer parent for longest period.

rule tiebreaker_treats_individual_as_qualifying_child_of_taxpayer_4 with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(4)":
a person is tiebreaker treats individual as qualifying child of taxpayer if
    the individual of the person may be claimed as qualifying child by two or more taxpayers
    and it is not the case that the parents of individual of the person may claim individual but no parent claims
    and the person is parents claiming child do not file joint return together
    and the taxpayer of the person is parent of individual
    and the child resided with both parents same amount of time and taxpayer parent of the person has highest adjusted gross income.

rule tiebreaker_treats_individual_as_qualifying_child_of_taxpayer_5 with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(4)":
a person is tiebreaker treats individual as qualifying child of taxpayer if
    the individual of the person may be claimed as qualifying child by two or more taxpayers
    and it is not the case that the parents of individual of the person may claim individual but no parent claims
    and it is not the case that the person is parents claiming child do not file joint return together
    and the taxpayer of the person is parent of individual.

rule tiebreaker_treats_individual_as_qualifying_child_of_taxpayer_6 with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(4)":
a person is tiebreaker treats individual as qualifying child of taxpayer if
    the individual of the person may be claimed as qualifying child by two or more taxpayers
    and it is not the case that the parents of individual of the person may claim individual but no parent claims
    and it is not the case that the person is parents claiming child do not file joint return together
    and the no parent of individual of the person is claiming taxpayer
    and the taxpayer of the person has highest adjusted gross income among claiming taxpayers.

rule qualifying_child with provenance "26 USC 152(c)(1), 152(c)(4)":
a person is qualifying child if
    the person is qualifying child before tiebreaker
    and the person is tiebreaker treats individual as qualifying child of taxpayer.


