rule possession_is_specified_possession_1 with provenance "26 USC 931(c)":
the possession of a tax unit is specified possession if
    the possession of the tax unit is guam.

rule possession_is_specified_possession_2 with provenance "26 USC 931(c)":
the possession of a tax unit is specified possession if
    the possession of the tax unit is american samoa.

rule possession_is_specified_possession_3 with provenance "26 USC 931(c)":
the possession of a tax unit is specified possession if
    the possession of the tax unit is northern mariana islands.

rule amount_excluded_from_gross_income_under_section_931 with provenance "26 USC 931(a), 931(d)":
the amount excluded from gross income under section 931 of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the tax unit is bona fide resident of specified possession during entire taxable year
    and the income derived from sources within specified possessions of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the income effectively connected with trade or business within specified possessions of the tax unit is an amount K
    and the amounts paid for services as employee of united states or agency of the tax unit is a value V
    and a number P = M + K - V
    and the maximum of 0 and P is N
    otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
    and N = 0.

rule section_931_disallowed_deductions_excluding_section_151 with provenance "26 USC 931(b)(1)":
the section 931 disallowed deductions excluding section 151 of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the deductions other than section 151 before section 931 denial of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the deductions properly allocable or chargeable to amounts excluded under section 931 of the tax unit is an amount K
    and the maximum of 0 and M is a number P
    and the maximum of 0 and K is a number Q
    and the minimum of P and Q is N.

rule deductions_other_than_section_151_allowed_after_section_931 with provenance "26 USC 931(b)(1)":
the deductions other than section 151 allowed after section 931 of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the deductions other than section 151 before section 931 denial of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the section 931 disallowed deductions excluding section 151 of the tax unit is an amount K
    and a number P = M - K
    and the maximum of 0 and P is N.

rule section_931_disallowed_credits with provenance "26 USC 931(b)(2)":
the section 931 disallowed credits of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the credits before section 931 denial of the tax unit is a value V
    and the credits properly allocable or chargeable to amounts excluded under section 931 of the tax unit is a value M
    and the maximum of 0 and V is a number K
    and the maximum of 0 and M is a number P
    and the minimum of K and P is N.

rule credits_allowed_after_section_931 with provenance "26 USC 931(b)(2)":
the credits allowed after section 931 of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the credits before section 931 denial of the tax unit is a value V
    and the section 931 disallowed credits of the tax unit is an amount M
    and a number K = V - M
    and the maximum of 0 and K is N.


