the puerto rico residence before change minimum years is 2, as stated in "26 USC 933(2)".

rule entire_year_puerto_rico_source_income_excluded with provenance "26 USC 933(1)":
the entire year puerto rico source income excluded of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the individual of the tax unit is bona fide resident of puerto rico during entire taxable year
    and the income derived from sources within puerto rico of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the amounts received for services performed as employee of united states or agency of the tax unit is a value V
    and a number K = M - V
    and the maximum of 0 and K is N
    otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
    and N = 0.

rule change_year_puerto_rico_source_income_excluded with provenance "26 USC 933(2)":
the change year puerto rico source income excluded of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the individual of the tax unit is citizen of united states
    and the tax unit is individual changes residence from puerto rico during taxable year
    and the bona fide resident of puerto rico years before change of the tax unit is a number M
    and the puerto rico residence before change minimum years is a number K
    and M >= K
    and the puerto rico source income attributable to puerto rican residence period before change of the tax unit is an amount P
    and the amounts received for services performed as employee of united states or agency attributable to period before change of the tax unit is a value V
    and a number Q = P - V
    and the maximum of 0 and Q is N
    otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
    and N = 0.

rule income_excluded_from_gross_income_under_section_933 with provenance "26 USC 933(1), 933(2)":
the income excluded from gross income under section 933 of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the entire year puerto rico source income excluded of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the change year puerto rico source income excluded of the tax unit is an amount K
    and N = M + K.

rule section_933_disallowed_deductions_other_than_section_151 with provenance "26 USC 933(1), 933(2)":
the section 933 disallowed deductions other than section 151 of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the income excluded from gross income under section 933 of the tax unit is an amount M
    and M > 0
    and the deductions other than section 151 before section 933 denial of the tax unit is an amount K
    and the deductions other than section 151 properly allocable or chargeable to amounts excluded under section 933 of the tax unit is an amount P
    and the minimum of K and P is N
    otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
    and N = 0.

rule section_933_disallowed_credits with provenance "26 USC 933(1), 933(2)":
the section 933 disallowed credits of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the income excluded from gross income under section 933 of the tax unit is an amount M
    and M > 0
    and the credits before section 933 denial of the tax unit is a value V
    and the credits properly allocable or chargeable to amounts excluded under section 933 of the tax unit is a value K
    and the minimum of V and K is N
    otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
    and N = 0.


