rule statutory_exemption_amount_base with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(1)":
the statutory exemption amount base is 2000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule exemption_phaseout_rate_per_increment with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(3)(B)":
the exemption phaseout rate per increment is 0.02 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule exemption_phaseout_increment with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(3)(B)":
the exemption phaseout increment is 2500 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule exemption_phaseout_increment_separate with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(3)(B)":
the exemption phaseout increment separate is 1250 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule exemption_phaseout_maximum_percentage with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(3)(B)":
the exemption phaseout maximum percentage is 1 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule post_2017_exemption_amount with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(5)(A)":
the post 2017 exemption amount is 0 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule senior_deduction_base_amount with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(5)(C)(i)":
the senior deduction base amount is 6000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule senior_deduction_age_threshold with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(5)(C)(ii)":
the senior deduction age threshold is 65 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule senior_deduction_phaseout_rate with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(5)(C)(iii)(I)":
the senior deduction phaseout rate is 0.06 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule senior_deduction_phaseout_threshold_other with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(5)(C)(iii)(I)":
the senior deduction phaseout threshold other is 75000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule senior_deduction_phaseout_threshold_joint with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(5)(C)(iii)(I)":
the senior deduction phaseout threshold joint is 150000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule exemption_amount with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(1), 151(d)(5)(A)":
the exemption amount of a tax unit is an amount if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is taxable year begins after exemption amount zero start
        and the post 2017 exemption amount is the amount
        otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
        and the statutory exemption amount base is the amount.

rule exemption_individual_eligible_1 with provenance "26 USC 151(b), 151(e)":
a person is exemption individual eligible if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the person is tin included on return claiming exemption
    and the person is taxpayer.

rule exemption_individual_eligible_2 with provenance "26 USC 151(b), 151(e)":
a person is exemption individual eligible if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the person is tin included on return claiming exemption
    and the person is spouse of taxpayer
    and it is not the case that
        the filing status of the person is a code C
        and C = 1
    and the spouse of the person has no gross income for calendar year
    and it is not the case that the spouse of the person is dependent of another taxpayer.

rule section_151_exemption_deduction with provenance "26 USC 151(a), 151(b), 151(c), 151(d)(5)(A), 151(e)":
the section 151 exemption deduction of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the taxpayer of the tax unit is individual
        and the exemption amount of the tax unit is an amount M
        and a number K is the count of each P such that
            a person P is a exemption individual of the tax unit
        and a number R is the count of each Q such that
            a person Q is a exemption individual of the tax unit
            and it is not the case that Q is exemption individual eligible
        and N = M * (K - R)
        otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
        and N = 0.

rule senior_deduction_qualified_individual_1 with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(5)(C)(ii), 151(d)(5)(C)(iv)":
the senior deduction of a person qualified individual if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the person qualified individual social security number included on return
    and the age of the person is a number N
    and the senior deduction age threshold is a number M
    and N >= M
    and the person is taxpayer.

rule senior_deduction_qualified_individual_2 with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(5)(C)(ii), 151(d)(5)(C)(iv)":
the senior deduction of a person qualified individual if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the person qualified individual social security number included on return
    and the age of the person is a number N
    and the senior deduction age threshold is a number M
    and N >= M
    and the person is spouse of taxpayer
    and the filing status of the person is a code C
    and C = 1.

rule senior_deduction_modified_adjusted_gross_income with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(5)(C)(iii)(II)":
the senior deduction modified adjusted gross income of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the adjusted gross income of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the section 911 amount excluded from gross income of the tax unit is an amount K
    and the amount excluded from gross income under section 931 of the tax unit is an amount P
    and the income excluded from gross income under section 933 of the tax unit is an amount Q
    and a number R = M + K + P + Q
    and the maximum of 0 and R is N.

rule senior_deduction_phaseout_threshold with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(5)(C)(iii)(I)":
the senior deduction phaseout threshold of a tax unit is an amount if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the filing status of the tax unit is a code C
        and C = 1
        and the senior deduction phaseout threshold joint is the amount
        otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
        and the senior deduction phaseout threshold other is the amount.

rule senior_deduction_amount_per_qualified_individual with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(5)(C)(i), 151(d)(5)(C)(iii)(I)":
the senior deduction amount per qualified individual of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the senior deduction base amount is an amount M
    and the senior deduction phaseout rate is a rate R
    and the senior deduction modified adjusted gross income of the tax unit is an amount K
    and the senior deduction phaseout threshold of the tax unit is an amount P
    and a number Q = K - P
    and the maximum of 0 and Q is a number S
    and a number T = M - R * S
    and the maximum of 0 and T is N.

rule senior_deduction_eligible_1 with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(5)(C)(i), 151(d)(5)(C)(v)":
a tax unit is senior deduction eligible if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the taxpayer of the tax unit is individual
    and the tax unit is taxable year begins before senior deduction termination
    and it is not the case that
        the filing status of the tax unit is a code C
        and C = 1
    and it is not the case that
        the filing status of the tax unit is a code N
        and N = 2.

rule senior_deduction_eligible_2 with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(5)(C)(i), 151(d)(5)(C)(v)":
a tax unit is senior deduction eligible if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the taxpayer of the tax unit is individual
    and the tax unit is taxable year begins before senior deduction termination
    and the filing status of the tax unit is a code C
    and C = 1.

rule senior_deduction with provenance "26 USC 151(d)(5)(C)":
the senior deduction of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is senior deduction eligible
        and the senior deduction amount per qualified individual of the tax unit is an amount M
        and a number K is the count of each P such that
            a person P is a senior deduction individual of the tax unit
        and a number R is the count of each Q such that
            a person Q is a senior deduction individual of the tax unit
            and it is not the case that the senior deduction of Q qualified individual
        and N = M * (K - R)
        otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
        and N = 0.


