the child principal abode fraction threshold is a rate R if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and R = 1 / 2.

the household cost fraction threshold is a rate R if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and R = 1 / 2.

rule spouse_absence_period_months with provenance "26 USC 7703(b)(3)":
the spouse absence period months is 6 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule taxpayer_married_under_general_rule_1 with provenance "26 USC 7703(a)":
a tax unit is taxpayer married under general rule if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is spouse dies during taxable year
    and the tax unit is taxpayer married at time of spouse death
    and it is not the case that the tax unit is legally separated under decree of divorce or separate maintenance.

rule taxpayer_married_under_general_rule_2 with provenance "26 USC 7703(a)":
a tax unit is taxpayer married under general rule if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and it is not the case that the tax unit is spouse dies during taxable year
    and the tax unit is taxpayer married at close of taxable year
    and it is not the case that the tax unit is legally separated under decree of divorce or separate maintenance.

rule living_apart_child_has_required_abode_and_deduction_1 with provenance "26 USC 7703(b)(1)":
the living apart child of a person has required abode and deduction if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the person is child within federal tax child definition
    and the taxpayer household of the person is child principal place of abode
    and the child principal abode fraction of taxable year of the person is a number N
    and the child principal abode fraction threshold is a rate R
    and N > R
    and the person is exemption individual eligible.

rule living_apart_child_has_required_abode_and_deduction_2 with provenance "26 USC 7703(b)(1)":
the living apart child of a person has required abode and deduction if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the person is child within federal tax child definition
    and the taxpayer household of the person is child principal place of abode
    and the child principal abode fraction of taxable year of the person is a number N
    and the child principal abode fraction threshold is a rate R
    and N > R
    and the person would be entitled to child deduction but for parent release rule.

rule taxpayer_not_considered_married_when_living_apart with provenance "26 USC 7703(b)":
a tax unit is taxpayer not considered married when living apart if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is taxpayer married under general rule
    and the taxpayer of the tax unit files separate return
    and the tax unit is taxpayer maintains household as home
    and a number N is the count of each P such that
        a person P is a living apart child of the tax unit
    and a number K is the count of each M such that
        a person M is a living apart child of the tax unit
        and it is not the case that the living apart child of M has required abode and deduction
    and N - K > 0
    and the taxpayer household cost fraction furnished of the tax unit is a rate R
    and the household cost fraction threshold is a rate Q
    and R > Q
    and the spouse not member of household final month count of the tax unit is a number S
    and the spouse absence period months is a number T
    and S >= T.

rule taxpayer_considered_married_after_living_apart_rule with provenance "26 USC 7703(a), (b)":
a tax unit is taxpayer considered married after living apart rule if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is taxpayer married under general rule
    and it is not the case that the tax unit is taxpayer not considered married when living apart.


