rule eitc_childless_minimum_age with provenance "26 USC 32(c)(1)(A)(ii)(II)":
the eitc childless minimum age is 25 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule eitc_childless_age_ceiling_exclusive with provenance "26 USC 32(c)(1)(A)(ii)(II)":
the eitc childless age ceiling exclusive is 65 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule eitc_qualifying_child_base with provenance "26 USC 32(c)(3), 26 USC 152(c)":
a person is eitc qualifying child base if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the person is qualifying child relationship
    and the individual principal place of abode with taxpayer fraction of the person is a rate R
    and the abode fraction threshold is a number N
    and R > N
    and the person is age requirements met
    and it is not the case that the person is individual filed joint return with spouse other than only for claim of refund
    and the person is tiebreaker treats individual as qualifying child of taxpayer.

rule eitc_qualifying_child_1 with provenance "26 USC 32(c)(3)":
a person is eitc qualifying child if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the person is eitc qualifying child base
    and the qualifying child principal place of abode of the person is in united states
    and the person is qualifying child name age and tin included on return
    and it is not the case that the qualifying child marital status of the person requires section 151 entitlement.

rule eitc_qualifying_child_2 with provenance "26 USC 32(c)(3)":
a person is eitc qualifying child if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the person is eitc qualifying child base
    and the qualifying child principal place of abode of the person is in united states
    and the person is qualifying child name age and tin included on return
    and the taxpayer entitled to section 151 deduction for child or of the person would be but for section 152 e.

rule eitc_child_count with provenance "26 USC 32(b)(1), 32(c)(3)":
the eitc child count of a tax unit is a number N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is a tax_unit
    and a number M is the count of each P such that
        a person P is a qualifying child of the tax unit
    and a number Q is the count of each K such that
        a person K is a qualifying child of the tax unit
        and it is not the case that K is eitc qualifying child
    and N = M - Q.

rule eitc_capped_child_count with provenance "26 USC 32(b)(1)":
the eitc capped child count of a tax unit is a number N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the eitc child count of the tax unit is a number M
    and the minimum of M and 3 is N.

rule eitc_phase_in_rate with provenance "26 USC 32(b)(1)":
the eitc phase in rate of a tax unit is a rate if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number N
        and N = 0
        and the eitc phase in rates for 0 is the rate
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number M
        and M = 1
        and the eitc phase in rates for 1 is the rate
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number K
        and K = 2
        and the eitc phase in rates for 2 is the rate
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number P
        and P = 3
        and the eitc phase in rates for 3 is the rate.

rule eitc_phase_out_rate with provenance "26 USC 32(b)(1)":
the eitc phase out rate of a tax unit is a rate if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number N
        and N = 0
        and the eitc phase out rates for 0 is the rate
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number M
        and M = 1
        and the eitc phase out rates for 1 is the rate
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number K
        and K = 2
        and the eitc phase out rates for 2 is the rate
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number P
        and P = 3
        and the eitc phase out rates for 3 is the rate.

rule eitc_earned_income_amount with provenance "26 USC 32(b)(2), 32(j)":
the eitc earned income amount of a tax unit is an amount if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number N
        and N = 0
        and the eitc earned income amounts for 0 is the amount
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number M
        and M = 1
        and the eitc earned income amounts for 1 is the amount
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number K
        and K = 2
        and the eitc earned income amounts for 2 is the amount
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number P
        and P = 3
        and the eitc earned income amounts for 3 is the amount.

rule eitc_maximum with provenance "26 USC 32(a)(2)(A), 32(b)(1), 32(b)(2)":
the eitc maximum of a tax unit is an amount if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number N
        and N = 0
        and the eitc maximum credit amounts for 0 is the amount
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number M
        and M = 1
        and the eitc maximum credit amounts for 1 is the amount
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number K
        and K = 2
        and the eitc maximum credit amounts for 2 is the amount
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number P
        and P = 3
        and the eitc maximum credit amounts for 3 is the amount.

rule eitc_phase_out_start with provenance "26 USC 32(b)(2), 32(j)":
the eitc phase out start of a tax unit is an amount if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the filing status of the tax unit is a code C
        and C = 1
        and the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number N
        and N = 0
        and the eitc threshold phaseout amounts joint for 0 is the amount
        otherwise the filing status of the tax unit is C
        and C = 1
        and the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number M
        and M = 1
        and the eitc threshold phaseout amounts joint for 1 is the amount
        otherwise the filing status of the tax unit is C
        and C = 1
        and the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number K
        and K = 2
        and the eitc threshold phaseout amounts joint for 2 is the amount
        otherwise the filing status of the tax unit is C
        and C = 1
        and the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number P
        and P = 3
        and the eitc threshold phaseout amounts joint for 3 is the amount
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number Q
        and Q = 0
        and the eitc threshold phaseout amounts other for 0 is the amount
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number R
        and R = 1
        and the eitc threshold phaseout amounts other for 1 is the amount
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number S
        and S = 2
        and the eitc threshold phaseout amounts other for 2 is the amount
        otherwise the eitc capped child count of the tax unit is a number T
        and T = 3
        and the eitc threshold phaseout amounts other for 3 is the amount.

rule eitc_phase_out_income with provenance "26 USC 32(a)(2)(B)":
the eitc phase out income of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the adjusted gross income of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the earned income of the tax unit is an amount K
    and the maximum of M and K is N.

rule eitc_phased_in with provenance "26 USC 32(a)(1)":
the eitc phased in of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the earned income of the tax unit is an amount M
        and the eitc earned income amount of the tax unit is an amount K
        and M >= K
        and the eitc maximum of the tax unit is N
        otherwise the eitc phase in rate of the tax unit is a rate R
        and the earned income of the tax unit is an amount P
        and the eitc earned income amount of the tax unit is an amount Q
        and the maximum of 0 and P is a number S
        and the minimum of S and Q is a number T
        and N = R * T.

rule eitc_reduction with provenance "26 USC 32(a)(2)(B)":
the eitc reduction of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the eitc phase out rate of the tax unit is a rate R
    and the eitc phase out income of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the eitc phase out start of the tax unit is an amount K
    and a number P = M - K
    and the maximum of 0 and P is a number Q
    and N = R * Q.

rule eitc_before_eligibility with provenance "26 USC 32(a)":
the eitc before eligibility of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the eitc phased in of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the eitc maximum of the tax unit is an amount K
    and the eitc reduction of the tax unit is an amount P
    and a number Q = K - P
    and the minimum of M and Q is a number R
    and the maximum of 0 and R is N.

rule eitc_childless_age_eligible with provenance "26 USC 32(c)(1)(A)(ii)(II)":
a person is eitc childless age eligible if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the age of the person is a number N
    and the eitc childless minimum age is a number M
    and N >= M
    and the age of the person is a number K
    and the eitc childless age ceiling exclusive is a number P
    and K < P.

rule eitc_demographic_eligible with provenance "26 USC 32(c)(1)(A)-(D), 32(d), 32(e), 32(k)":
a tax unit is eitc demographic eligible if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the eitc child count of the tax unit is a number N
        and N > 0
        or the tax unit is childless taxpayer principal place of abode in united states more than half year
            and the tax unit is childless taxpayer or spouse age eligible for eitc
            and it is not the case that the taxpayer of the tax unit is dependent for section 151 to another taxpayer
    and it is not the case that the taxpayer of the tax unit is qualifying child of another taxpayer
    and it is not the case that the taxpayer of the tax unit claims section 911 benefits
    and the tax unit is taxpayer treated as resident by section 6013 g or h election
        or it is not the case that the taxpayer of the tax unit is nonresident alien for any portion of year
    and the filing status of the tax unit is a code C
        and C = 1
        or it is not the case that the tax unit is taxpayer married under general rule
        or the tax unit satisfies eitc separated spouse rules
    and the taxable year of the tax unit is full 12 months
        or the tax unit is taxable year closed by reason of taxpayer death
    and it is not the case that the eitc disallowance period of the tax unit applies
    and it is not the case that the tax unit is prior deficiency denial without required eligibility information.

rule eitc_identification_requirements_satisfied_1 with provenance "26 USC 32(c)(1)(E), 26 USC 32(m)":
a tax unit is eitc identification requirements satisfied if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the taxpayer of the tax unit includes required social security number on return
    and it is not the case that the tax unit is taxpayer married under general rule.

rule eitc_identification_requirements_satisfied_2 with provenance "26 USC 32(c)(1)(E), 26 USC 32(m)":
a tax unit is eitc identification requirements satisfied if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the taxpayer of the tax unit includes required social security number on return
    and the spouse of the tax unit includes required social security number on return.

rule eitc_investment_income_eligible with provenance "26 USC 32(i), 32(j)":
a tax unit is eitc investment income eligible if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the eitc relevant investment income of the tax unit is an amount N
    and the eitc maximum investment income is an amount M
    and N <= M.

rule eitc_allowed with provenance "26 USC 32(a), 32(c)(1)(E), 32(i), 32(k)":
a tax unit is eitc allowed if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is eitc demographic eligible
    and the tax unit is eitc identification requirements satisfied
    and the tax unit is eitc investment income eligible.

rule eitc with provenance "26 USC 32(a), 32(c)(1)(E), 32(i), 32(k)":
the eitc of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is eitc allowed
        and the eitc before eligibility of the tax unit is N
        otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
        and N = 0.


