the text of "26 USC 24(d)(1)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/24/d.yaml".

rule ctc_refundable_phase_in_rate with provenance "26 USC 24(d)(1)(B)(i)":
the ctc refundable phase in rate is 0.15 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_refundable_phase_in_threshold with provenance "26 USC 24(d)(1)(B)(i)":
the ctc refundable phase in threshold is 3000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_refundable_min_children_for_ss_excess with provenance "26 USC 24(d)(1)(B)(ii)":
the ctc refundable min children for ss excess is 3 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_social_security_half_share with provenance "26 USC 24(d)(2)(A)(ii)-(iii)":
the ctc social security half share is 0.5 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_phase_in_earned_income_base with provenance "26 USC 24(d)(1)(B)(i)":
the ctc phase in earned income base of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the earned income before section 112 election of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the amount excluded from gross income by reason of section 112 of the tax unit is an amount K
    and N = M + K.

rule ctc_phase_in_relevant_earnings with provenance "26 USC 24(d)(1)(B)(i)":
the ctc phase in relevant earnings of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the ctc refundable phase in rate is a rate R
    and the ctc phase in earned income base of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the ctc refundable phase in threshold is an amount K
    and a number P = M - K
    and the maximum of 0 and P is a number Q
    and N = R * Q.

rule ctc_social_security_tax with provenance "26 USC 24(d)(2)":
the ctc social security tax of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the employee 3101 3201 a taxes of the tax unit is a value V
    and the american employer foreign affiliate equivalent 3121 l taxes of the tax unit is a value M
    and the ctc social security half share is a rate R
    and the self employment 1401 taxes of the tax unit is a value K
    and the railroad 3211 a taxes of the tax unit is a value P
    and the special refund social security taxes under 6413 c of the tax unit is a value Q
    and a number S = V + M + R * K + R * P - Q
    and the maximum of 0 and S is N.

rule ctc_social_security_excess with provenance "26 USC 24(d)(1)(B)(ii)":
the ctc social security excess of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the qualifying children count of the tax unit is a number M
        and the ctc refundable min children for ss excess is a number K
        and M >= K
        and the ctc social security tax of the tax unit is an amount P
        and the eitc of the tax unit is an amount Q
        and a number R = P - Q
        and the maximum of 0 and R is N
        otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
        and N = 0.

rule ctc_refundable_limitation_increase_amount with provenance "26 USC 24(d)(1)(B)":
the ctc refundable limitation increase amount of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the ctc phase in relevant earnings of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the ctc social security excess of the tax unit is an amount K
    and the maximum of M and K is N.

rule ctc_refundable_tax_increase with provenance "26 USC 24(d)(1)(B)":
the ctc refundable tax increase of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the aggregate subpart c credits with increased 26 a limit of the tax unit is a value V
    and the aggregate subpart c credits without subsection of the tax unit is a value M
    and a number K = V - M
    and the maximum of 0 and K is N.

rule ctc_refundable_cap with provenance "26 USC 24(d)(1)(A)":
the ctc refundable cap of a tax unit is an amount if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the ctc credit without subsection and 26 a limit of the tax unit is the amount.

rule ctc_refundable_foreign_income_eligible with provenance "26 USC 24(d)(3)":
a tax unit is ctc refundable foreign income eligible if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is a tax_unit
    and it is not the case that the tax unit elects foreign earned income exclusion under 911.

rule refundable_ctc with provenance "26 USC 24(d)(1)":
the refundable ctc of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is ctc refundable foreign income eligible
        and the ctc refundable cap of the tax unit is an amount M
        and the ctc refundable limitation increase amount of the tax unit is an amount K
        and the ctc refundable tax increase of the tax unit is an amount P
        and the minimum of K and P is a number Q
        and the minimum of M and Q is N
        otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
        and N = 0.

rule non_refundable_ctc with provenance "26 USC 24(d)(1)":
the non refundable ctc of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2026-01-01 <= D
    and the ctc credit without subsection and 26 a limit of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the refundable ctc of the tax unit is an amount K
    and a number P = M - K
